<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles III William, Margrave of Baden-Durlach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1679–1738</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Charles III William</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles III William was Margrave of Baden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durlach">Durlach</a> from 1709. In 1715 he founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlsruhe">Karlsruhe</a> as his new residence, laid out with streets radiating from the palace tower like the ribs of a fan. He offered religious toleration and privileges to attract settlers, and Karlsruhe later became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-iii-william-margrave-of-baden-durlach.jpg" alt="Charles III William, Margrave of Baden-Durlach" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Rudolf Huber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huber_Carl_III.Wilhelm.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
